# MCP-Playwright Integration

This project integrates Model Context Protocol (MCP) with Playwright for browser automation. It follows a server-client architecture where browser automation tasks are executed through MCP tools.

## Key Components

### Main Integration File
The [expiremental-new.py](mdc:expiremental-new.py) file contains both the MCP server and client implementation integrated into a single file. It handles:
- MCP server setup and initialization
- Client-side communication
- Natural language processing for browser automation
- Tool execution planning

### Playwright Tools
The [exp_tools.py](mdc:exp_tools.py) contains the implementation of various Playwright tools that are exposed to the MCP server. These tools include:
- Browser navigation and interaction
- Element selection and manipulation
- Screenshot and content extraction
- Advanced multi-strategy approaches for handling complex UI interactions

## Architecture

The system is built as a Model Context Protocol server using the [python-sdk](mdc:https:/github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk) from the Model Context Protocol project. It exposes Playwright browser automation capabilities as MCP tools that can be called by clients.

### Key Classes
- `PlaywrightMCPServer`: Handles server-side MCP implementation
- `MCPClient`: Handles client-side communication and tool discovery
- `PlaywrightTools`: Contains the actual browser automation tool implementations

## Workflow
1. The server exposes Playwright tools via MCP
2. Natural language commands are processed by an LLM
3. Commands are converted to structured tool calls
4. Tool calls are executed on the browser
5. Results are returned to the client

